<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#mounted-archer">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mounted archer</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as mounted archers</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A mounted archer is a cavalry soldier who shoots arrows from horseback. Mounted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/archery">archers</a> were the foundation of steppe military power, combining mobility with firepower. They were central to the armies of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khazar-khaganate">Khazar Khaganate</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khwarazmian-empire">Khwarazmian Empire</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a>.</p></div>
